homelab-cli (0.2.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add `mail search`, `mail flags`, `mail move`, `mail trash`, `mail
    purge`, and `mail folder-create`/`folder-rename`/`folder-delete`
    commands, wrapping the new mutating mail endpoints. `trash` moves a
    message to the account's Trash (recoverable); `purge` permanently
    deletes a message but only works on one already in Trash and has no
    --folder option, since it can never target a live mailbox.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:00:00 -0500

homelab-cli (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add `mail folders`, `mail messages`, `mail message`, and `mail part`
    commands, wrapping the new GET /api/v1/mail/{folders,messages,
    messages/:uid,messages/:uid/part} endpoints. A message's content is
    exposed as a flat list of MIME parts (no single "body" field) --
    `mail part` fetches any specific part's content by number, text or
    binary alike. Updated homelab-cli-mail(8).

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Fri, 21 Aug 2026 19:15:00 -0500

homelab-cli (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release v0.2.1

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Fri, 21 Aug 2026 18:31:02 -0500

homelab-cli (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BREAKING: replace flat subcommands with grouped `<group> <command>`
    invocation (e.g. `quota` -> `drive quota`, `admin-list-roles` ->
    `admin list-roles`). No backward-compatible aliases for old command
    names. Man page split into homelab-cli(8) (overview) plus
    homelab-cli-drive(8) and homelab-cli-admin(8) (per-group reference).
  * Add `mail status` command (new `mail` group), showing INBOX
    unseen/total message counts via the new GET /api/v1/mail/status
    endpoint. New homelab-cli-mail(8) man page.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:53:20 -0500

